1
00:01:40,644 --> 00:01:43,647
This is Kameari Park Police Station.

2
00:01:44,715 --> 00:01:48,085
I see. So this is the infamous...

3
00:01:52,122 --> 00:01:53,356
"BIG SUMMER SALE"

4
00:01:57,360 --> 00:02:00,664
...Kameari Park Police Station.

5
00:02:01,832 --> 00:02:02,632
Well, well.

6
00:02:04,334 --> 00:02:08,672
Community police work is a foundational pillar of society.

7
00:02:09,272 --> 00:02:10,006
We prevent—

8
00:02:10,207 --> 00:02:11,942
Yes, we prevent crime.

9
00:02:12,142 --> 00:02:17,347
We also see higher incarceration rates through regular questioning on patrol.

10
00:02:18,615 --> 00:02:22,119
Police Academy Handbook, page 777.

11
00:02:23,320 --> 00:02:26,356
Let's do introductions. This is Miyaji, our new trainee.

12
00:02:28,125 --> 00:02:28,825
Hello.

13
00:02:29,025 --> 00:02:30,293
Nice to meet you.

14
00:02:30,760 --> 00:02:33,096
Miyaji graduated from Tojo University.

15
00:02:33,296 --> 00:02:36,032
He entered the police academy with top grades.

16
00:02:36,233 --> 00:02:39,035
He was personally recommended for his performance.

17
00:02:39,369 --> 00:02:40,570
Wow!

18
00:02:40,804 --> 00:02:43,340
Isn't Tojo University pretty prestigious?

19
00:02:43,540 --> 00:02:46,143
Yeah. No doubt he's in line for leadership.

20
00:02:46,343 --> 00:02:48,111
Terai's one of our officers.

21
00:02:48,311 --> 00:02:50,781
Feel free to come to me with any questions.

22
00:02:51,181 --> 00:02:53,350
I won't be doing that. I know everything.

23
00:02:53,550 --> 00:02:56,052
Even if I didn't, I wouldn't ask you.

24
00:02:56,253 --> 00:02:57,053
Eh...

25
00:02:58,688 --> 00:03:00,891
Now, now. Let's all play nice.

26
00:03:01,525 --> 00:03:04,861
Then we have Nakagawa, and our sole female officer, Reiko.

27
00:03:05,061 --> 00:03:05,796
Hello.

28
00:03:06,696 --> 00:03:10,167
It's an honor to have such an outstanding trainee join us.

29
00:03:10,367 --> 00:03:11,134
Hmm?

30
00:03:13,236 --> 00:03:16,406
Police Academy Handbook, page 124.

31
00:03:16,606 --> 00:03:18,909
The section on uniform requirements.

32
00:03:19,142 --> 00:03:22,913
Anything other than the prescribed uniform is prohibited, Nakagawa.

33
00:03:23,146 --> 00:03:25,048
Yes... That's true.

34
00:03:25,549 --> 00:03:27,350
I did get permission, though.

35
00:03:27,551 --> 00:03:30,687
Who wants to wear the same uniform as everyone else?

36
00:03:35,091 --> 00:03:37,427
20 centimeters above the knee. Far too short.

37
00:03:38,528 --> 00:03:41,031
Yellow and pink uniforms are inappropriate.

38
00:03:41,231 --> 00:03:41,932
Chief Ohara!

39
00:03:42,265 --> 00:03:43,533
What is it?

40
00:03:43,733 --> 00:03:47,938
Do you know what they say about this station at the police academy?

41
00:03:48,171 --> 00:03:48,939
Uh, no...

42
00:03:49,172 --> 00:03:53,577
Kameari Park Police Station is the black sheep of the Katsushika Precinct.

43
00:03:54,277 --> 00:03:56,213
It's where they dump underachievers.

44
00:03:58,114 --> 00:04:00,550
There are also issues with your management.

45
00:04:03,486 --> 00:04:07,624
I cannot fathom why the first step in my illustrious career should be here.

46
00:04:07,858 --> 00:04:10,293
Who knows what those higher-ups are thinking.

47
00:04:13,463 --> 00:04:18,301
I'll create my own training schedule, so you may leave me be.

48
00:04:21,771 --> 00:04:24,875
Terada-san. Will you fetch me a map of the patrol area?

49
00:04:25,275 --> 00:04:26,309
Oh, sure.

50
00:04:28,612 --> 00:04:29,980
Um...

51
00:04:30,213 --> 00:04:31,481
It's actually Terai.

52
00:04:31,982 --> 00:04:33,083
Sure. Thanks.

53
00:04:37,287 --> 00:04:40,223
What a pain in the backside this new trainee is.

54
00:04:40,423 --> 00:04:42,092
At least it's only for one day.

55
00:04:42,292 --> 00:04:44,828
I think it's going to be a long day.

56
00:04:45,061 --> 00:04:47,230
Yahoo!

57
00:04:50,066 --> 00:04:50,767
Yeah!

58
00:04:51,234 --> 00:04:53,069
Good morning at 100 km/h!

59
00:04:53,503 --> 00:04:56,673
Sliding in with some sharp moves!

60
00:04:57,908 --> 00:04:59,075
Yeah!

61
00:05:01,378 --> 00:05:02,679
Morning!

62
00:05:03,013 --> 00:05:03,780
Ryo-chan!

63
00:05:04,347 --> 00:05:09,286
Would you believe it? My bike got a puncture first thing in the morning.

64
00:05:09,486 --> 00:05:11,288
And I've never ridden this thing.

65
00:05:11,788 --> 00:05:14,124
Cornering is my life!

66
00:05:14,324 --> 00:05:17,527
You! You made me lose all my important data!

67
00:05:18,295 --> 00:05:20,497
Yes, you may be wearing the correct uniform,

68
00:05:20,697 --> 00:05:24,801
but the Police Academy Handbook, page 125, gives supplementary provisions

69
00:05:25,268 --> 00:05:28,305
stating that all types of sandals are prohibited.

70
00:05:28,505 --> 00:05:29,973
-What is your name? -Me?

71
00:05:30,173 --> 00:05:32,042
I'm Kankichi Ryotsu. And you are?

72
00:05:32,275 --> 00:05:33,877
Hey, good morning, Ryotsu.

73
00:05:34,110 --> 00:05:36,112
Always in high spirits in the mornings.

74
00:05:36,313 --> 00:05:39,115
What's with this guy? He's giving me a headache.

75
00:05:39,582 --> 00:05:42,752
-This is Miyaji. He's a trainee. -A trainee?

76
00:05:42,986 --> 00:05:47,757
Head Patrol Officer Ryotsu, I'm appointing you as Miyaji's supervisor for the day.

77
00:05:47,991 --> 00:05:48,992
What?!

78
00:05:49,492 --> 00:05:52,729
What exactly am I supposed to do as his supervisor, Chief?

79
00:05:53,430 --> 00:05:56,599
Take him out on patrol. You can do that, right?

80
00:05:56,833 --> 00:05:59,135
Chief. I can do that on my own.

81
00:05:59,336 --> 00:06:01,571
This is an order from your chief, Miyaji.

82
00:06:02,205 --> 00:06:04,207
What page are the Service Regulations?

83
00:06:04,874 --> 00:06:07,877
Page 572, Section 17 of the Service Regulations.

84
00:06:08,078 --> 00:06:10,914
"You must obey the orders of your superior officers."

85
00:06:12,082 --> 00:06:13,550
Damn it.

86
00:06:13,750 --> 00:06:17,854
Today's the day Virtual Fantasy X arrives at the arcade.

87
00:06:18,054 --> 00:06:21,591
If I can just get rid of the trainee, I can play it all I want.

88
00:06:22,225 --> 00:06:24,928
All right, let's get moving. Follow me, trainee!

89
00:06:25,328 --> 00:06:26,896
R-Ryotsu-san!

90
00:06:27,097 --> 00:06:28,898
Keep up, trainee!

91
00:06:29,099 --> 00:06:33,436
Skateboards are not authorized equipment for patrol officers!

92
00:06:35,071 --> 00:06:38,274
Are you sure it's okay to leave Miyaji with Ryotsu, Chief?

93
00:06:38,475 --> 00:06:41,211
With Miyaji as the brain and Ryotsu as the brawn,

94
00:06:41,411 --> 00:06:45,248
their traits combined might lead to unexpectedly good results.

95
00:06:45,448 --> 00:06:48,218
Nice work on getting rid of them both, Chief.

96
00:06:48,418 --> 00:06:49,652
Ahem.

97
00:06:55,825 --> 00:06:56,493
Hmm?

98
00:06:57,627 --> 00:07:00,029
Ten minutes until the arcade opens.

99
00:07:02,265 --> 00:07:06,403
Mine is gonna be the first coin in the new game machine!

100
00:07:06,603 --> 00:07:07,604
-Ryotsu-san. -Huh?

101
00:07:08,238 --> 00:07:11,408
We seem to be deviating from the designated patrol route.

102
00:07:11,608 --> 00:07:12,842
We're fine.

103
00:07:13,076 --> 00:07:15,678
But the official route goes around the schools

104
00:07:15,912 --> 00:07:19,682
and then back toward Katsushika Police Headquarters.

105
00:07:20,316 --> 00:07:22,652
Why patrol around such boring places?

106
00:07:22,852 --> 00:07:26,523
My patrol route is arcades, pachinko parlors, and model shops!

107
00:07:26,756 --> 00:07:28,691
That's just a tour of the fun venues.

108
00:07:28,925 --> 00:07:30,627
Get back on the official route!

109
00:07:30,994 --> 00:07:33,263
If you don't like it, we can split up.

110
00:07:33,463 --> 00:07:35,799
You go that way, and I'll go this way.

111
00:07:35,999 --> 00:07:38,068
We'll meet back at the station in two hours.

112
00:07:38,268 --> 00:07:40,270
-See you. -Hold it right there.

113
00:07:40,804 --> 00:07:43,640
Page 843, New Recruit Training, Section 20.

114
00:07:43,840 --> 00:07:46,843
All patrols must be done alongside an active-duty officer.

115
00:07:47,077 --> 00:07:49,078
Who cares! Get out of the way!

116
00:07:50,180 --> 00:07:52,649
Are you disobeying your chief's orders?

117
00:07:52,849 --> 00:07:55,485
Are you shirking your supervisor responsibilities?

118
00:07:56,453 --> 00:08:01,257
I'm gonna miss out on being the first to play Virtual Fantasy X at this rate.

119
00:08:01,791 --> 00:08:02,959
Fine.

120
00:08:03,159 --> 00:08:06,029
To the official route we go.

121
00:08:06,663 --> 00:08:07,363
Huh?

122
00:08:12,168 --> 00:08:14,137
I'll give him the slip when I can.

123
00:08:15,538 --> 00:08:17,874
-Kameari Elementary School is clear. -Huh?!

124
00:08:21,377 --> 00:08:25,114
Hey, do you always carry books around like that?

125
00:08:25,315 --> 00:08:30,820
Yes. It is a habit that helped me get top grades in college and the police academy.

126
00:08:31,020 --> 00:08:34,891
Well, you need more than smarts to be a police officer.

127
00:08:35,125 --> 00:08:37,927
-One could say education is a hindrance. -What?

128
00:08:38,361 --> 00:08:40,930
A cop needs more than knowledge.

129
00:08:41,164 --> 00:08:43,933
He needs to make quick decisions and take action.

130
00:08:44,601 --> 00:08:46,069
Quick decisions?

131
00:08:47,370 --> 00:08:48,338
Ryotsu-san!

132
00:08:50,707 --> 00:08:52,408
Where are you going, Ryotsu-san?

133
00:08:52,942 --> 00:08:55,578
This was a quick decision! Remember that!

134
00:09:03,052 --> 00:09:04,053
Heck yeah!

135
00:09:05,855 --> 00:09:08,791
That was a costly loss of time. Only three minutes left.

136
00:09:09,025 --> 00:09:12,896
I might still have a chance if I rush in the moment the shutters open.

137
00:09:18,034 --> 00:09:18,902
Much faster!

138
00:09:19,102 --> 00:09:24,541
I'm gonna make a suggestion that we give each patrol officer a skateboard.

139
00:09:25,108 --> 00:09:27,210
30 seconds until it opens!

140
00:09:30,780 --> 00:09:32,081
Oh, it's opening.

141
00:09:32,649 --> 00:09:35,952
I'm excited for Virtual Fantasy X.

142
00:09:36,185 --> 00:09:37,520
Outta the way!

143
00:09:41,925 --> 00:09:43,526
Yes! I'm first!

144
00:09:44,527 --> 00:09:46,963
There it is. Virtual Fantasy X!

145
00:09:48,798 --> 00:09:49,532
Ryotsu-san!

146
00:09:50,200 --> 00:09:51,201
How did you know?

147
00:09:51,401 --> 00:09:54,203
I deduced that this was your likely destination!

148
00:09:56,406 --> 00:09:57,307
Oh no you don't!

149
00:10:00,376 --> 00:10:03,546
I'm gonna be first!

150
00:10:05,682 --> 00:10:07,383
Ha! Sucks to be you.

151
00:10:07,584 --> 00:10:08,585
Oh no!

152
00:10:17,460 --> 00:10:19,095
Hey! What did you do that for?

153
00:10:19,295 --> 00:10:20,597
Excuse me?

154
00:10:20,797 --> 00:10:25,501
I had to immediately violate the rules against acting alone because of you.

155
00:10:25,702 --> 00:10:27,837
Nobody will know if you just keep quiet.

156
00:10:28,037 --> 00:10:28,671
Huh?

157
00:10:29,238 --> 00:10:30,173
Well, I guess so.

158
00:10:34,677 --> 00:10:37,981
You wanted to play that so badly that you ran away from me?

159
00:10:38,781 --> 00:10:42,585
No, of course not. This is for patrol purposes.

160
00:10:42,785 --> 00:10:43,453
Huh?

161
00:10:44,187 --> 00:10:45,855
Police Duty Guidelines, Rule 30.

162
00:10:46,055 --> 00:10:48,825
"Patrol efficiently and cover a wide area."

163
00:10:49,025 --> 00:10:51,661
We must hurry or we won't be back in time.

164
00:10:52,595 --> 00:10:55,898
Ignore that. A pro trusts his instincts and focuses on one area.

165
00:10:56,132 --> 00:11:00,203
You pick a spot, and stick with it. That's how you do a real patrol.

166
00:11:00,436 --> 00:11:01,904
We'll be here for an hour.

167
00:11:04,073 --> 00:11:07,143
I've never heard of such a risky patrol strategy.

168
00:11:07,343 --> 00:11:08,044
Come on.

169
00:11:08,845 --> 00:11:10,046
We're leaving.

170
00:11:11,180 --> 00:11:13,049
Just one more go on that one!

171
00:11:13,516 --> 00:11:14,317
No.

172
00:11:27,363 --> 00:11:31,367
No suspicious vehicles or people. Nothing unusual to report.

173
00:11:31,567 --> 00:11:34,337
Just leave this to the traffic division.

174
00:11:35,104 --> 00:11:35,772
Hmm?

175
00:11:36,239 --> 00:11:37,640
Attention all units.

176
00:11:37,840 --> 00:11:42,078
Vandal apprehended at the arcade in the shopping district near the station.

177
00:11:42,312 --> 00:11:43,246
What?!

178
00:11:48,251 --> 00:11:50,053
Good work, boys!

179
00:11:57,226 --> 00:11:58,594
A change machine vandal...

180
00:11:58,795 --> 00:12:03,199
If we'd stayed here as I said, you would have made your first arrest.

181
00:12:03,700 --> 00:12:05,968
You missed out, Miyaji.

182
00:12:07,070 --> 00:12:09,339
Did you know a crime would take place?

183
00:12:09,906 --> 00:12:12,241
Sure did. I could smell it.

184
00:12:12,442 --> 00:12:17,046
As Head Patrol Officer, I can sniff out even the faintest scent of a crime.

185
00:12:17,246 --> 00:12:18,381
Crime has a scent?

186
00:12:18,748 --> 00:12:21,718
He's buying it. Now's my chance!

187
00:12:22,452 --> 00:12:27,590
Listen up. This isn't a skill you learn by sticking your nose in a book.

188
00:12:27,790 --> 00:12:30,693
Hmm? My nose is tingling again.

189
00:12:30,893 --> 00:12:32,161
Which way?

190
00:12:32,395 --> 00:12:33,096
This way!

191
00:12:33,296 --> 00:12:35,465
All right. Let's go, Miyaji!

192
00:12:35,698 --> 00:12:37,166
Yes, sir!

193
00:12:37,400 --> 00:12:38,801
"LUCKY PACHINKO"

194
00:12:41,637 --> 00:12:43,005
Is this the place?

195
00:12:43,239 --> 00:12:45,074
Yes. I can smell it.

196
00:12:45,475 --> 00:12:48,578
There's something going on in this pachinko parlor.

197
00:13:05,027 --> 00:13:06,796
It's always about the payout.

198
00:13:06,996 --> 00:13:10,099
A high score at the arcade won't pay for meals, after all.

199
00:13:10,500 --> 00:13:12,335
I've checked around the premises.

200
00:13:12,668 --> 00:13:14,403
Just when it was getting good...

201
00:13:14,604 --> 00:13:18,808
Did you send me on patrol just because you wanted some free time to play?

202
00:13:19,008 --> 00:13:21,878
You let a preventable crime slip through your fingers.

203
00:13:22,111 --> 00:13:24,347
You'll never understand my thinking.

204
00:13:24,947 --> 00:13:30,353
Even seated, I'm constantly monitoring the situation around me. Hmm?

205
00:13:35,758 --> 00:13:39,195
-Hey. That guy seems suspicious. -Huh?

206
00:13:39,796 --> 00:13:43,132
-Miyaji, go question him. -Huh?

207
00:13:43,499 --> 00:13:46,803
What happens with regular questioning on patrols?

208
00:13:47,003 --> 00:13:48,671
Higher incarceration rates!

209
00:13:48,871 --> 00:13:50,206
Okay sir, I'm on it!

210
00:13:53,242 --> 00:13:55,044
Excuse me.

211
00:13:55,511 --> 00:14:00,149
If you don't mind, can I ask what you do for a living?

212
00:14:00,683 --> 00:14:02,552
Hello? What is your occupation?

213
00:14:04,086 --> 00:14:05,054
My occupation?

214
00:14:05,621 --> 00:14:07,690
I'm asking what you do for a living!

215
00:14:09,058 --> 00:14:11,160
My occupation, huh?

216
00:14:13,162 --> 00:14:15,898
All right, here we go! Come to Poppa!

217
00:14:16,098 --> 00:14:16,933
What's that?

218
00:14:17,166 --> 00:14:19,068
Stop it!

219
00:14:19,936 --> 00:14:21,270
What the heck's going on?

220
00:14:21,504 --> 00:14:23,940
I don't know! I just asked him his occupation!

221
00:14:24,173 --> 00:14:24,841
Ouch, ouch, ouch!

222
00:14:25,174 --> 00:14:28,578
How pathetic. Did you not learn judo?

223
00:14:29,011 --> 00:14:31,013
I'm a third-dan, but...

224
00:14:31,914 --> 00:14:34,951
A third-dan can't even handle this kind of misbehavior?

225
00:14:35,818 --> 00:14:36,752
Hey, sir.

226
00:14:38,521 --> 00:14:39,755
Yuck!

227
00:14:40,189 --> 00:14:42,391
See that? You don't always need judo.

228
00:14:42,592 --> 00:14:45,728
Sometimes you just need the Hondara Fist Spit Dance.

229
00:14:45,928 --> 00:14:47,964
The Hondara Fist Spit Dance?

230
00:14:48,197 --> 00:14:50,266
Then when your opponent is stunned...

231
00:14:50,833 --> 00:14:53,603
Hondara Fist, Ear Yank!

232
00:14:54,370 --> 00:14:55,705
Take this!

233
00:14:55,905 --> 00:14:56,706
Oww!

234
00:14:58,507 --> 00:15:00,710
This is what I call improvisation.

235
00:15:03,279 --> 00:15:04,981
Got it, Miyaji?

236
00:15:05,448 --> 00:15:07,984
This looks like a suicide note.

237
00:15:08,217 --> 00:15:09,418
A suicide note?

238
00:15:09,752 --> 00:15:10,786
Were you...

239
00:15:11,520 --> 00:15:16,058
I got laid off from the company I worked at for the past thirty years.

240
00:15:18,294 --> 00:15:21,964
I'm sorry I lost my temper earlier.

241
00:15:22,431 --> 00:15:23,399
It's okay.

242
00:15:23,599 --> 00:15:25,968
Try not to let things get to you, all right?

243
00:15:26,168 --> 00:15:29,739
As long as you're alive, something good will come along eventually.

244
00:15:29,939 --> 00:15:31,908
Yes, thank you very much.

245
00:15:32,542 --> 00:15:33,442
Excuse me.

246
00:15:33,643 --> 00:15:34,810
Look after yourself.

247
00:15:35,177 --> 00:15:36,345
Cheer up!

248
00:15:36,879 --> 00:15:39,282
Is it okay to just leave him like that?

249
00:15:39,482 --> 00:15:43,352
Why not? He had the energy to choke you, so he'll be fine.

250
00:15:43,886 --> 00:15:48,357
He sensed a crime and saved a life all within one hour.

251
00:15:49,125 --> 00:15:52,929
Maybe this man is one of those rare, outstanding police officers.

252
00:15:54,096 --> 00:15:57,633
He said he got "laid," yeah? Isn't that typically a good thing?

253
00:15:58,267 --> 00:15:59,835
Or maybe not.

254
00:16:00,770 --> 00:16:03,839
Jeez, I'm starving after all that exercise.

255
00:16:09,045 --> 00:16:11,147
The dumplings here are always delicious.

256
00:16:11,747 --> 00:16:15,051
I'm sorry for asking you to do this, Ryo-san.

257
00:16:15,284 --> 00:16:16,385
Oh, thanks.

258
00:16:17,186 --> 00:16:20,289
But it's a good thing we happened to be passing by.

259
00:16:20,489 --> 00:16:22,625
You'd have been flooded if it rained.

260
00:16:23,059 --> 00:16:24,827
Heave-ho.

261
00:16:25,528 --> 00:16:28,464
This is no coincidence. You just came to eat dumplings.

262
00:16:29,065 --> 00:16:32,034
All comes with the job. Do it right, okay?

263
00:16:32,868 --> 00:16:37,206
What? Have I been wrong about anything I've said to you?

264
00:16:37,406 --> 00:16:41,377
You're too rigid-minded, and you lack practical experience.

265
00:16:41,611 --> 00:16:43,980
That's why you must work three times as hard.

266
00:16:46,616 --> 00:16:47,416
Do it properly!

267
00:16:54,223 --> 00:16:55,558
See? You did good.

268
00:16:56,225 --> 00:16:57,393
I can't even move.

269
00:16:57,626 --> 00:16:59,528
Sorry for all the trouble.

270
00:16:59,729 --> 00:17:03,432
Ryo-san, here's some bath tickets. Feel free to use them.

271
00:17:04,033 --> 00:17:08,571
You see, Miyaji? What goes around, comes around.

272
00:17:08,804 --> 00:17:11,807
Are public servants allowed to accept things like that?

273
00:17:12,008 --> 00:17:14,910
Would you have them waste someone's kindness?

274
00:17:15,111 --> 00:17:17,446
My quick decision is to take a bath!

275
00:17:17,680 --> 00:17:19,382
"MATSU NO YU BATHHOUSE"

276
00:17:21,017 --> 00:17:22,652
Ah, this is a nice bath.

277
00:17:23,352 --> 00:17:26,355
Are you sure we should be bathing while on duty?

278
00:17:26,555 --> 00:17:30,860
We're fine. It can't be pleasant being all dirty from cleaning the gutters.

279
00:17:31,060 --> 00:17:36,432
No, but I've already washed off the mud. Let's get back on patrol.

280
00:17:36,666 --> 00:17:39,301
All right, fine.

281
00:17:39,535 --> 00:17:42,471
But first, could you wash my back?

282
00:17:42,705 --> 00:17:44,940
-What? -Service Regulations, page 300.

283
00:17:45,141 --> 00:17:47,676
"You must obey the orders of your superior officers."

284
00:17:47,877 --> 00:17:49,445
It's page 572!

285
00:17:49,679 --> 00:17:50,379
Oh, whoops.

286
00:17:55,051 --> 00:17:56,452
Ah, that feels better.

287
00:17:56,685 --> 00:18:00,389
Now, remember. You can't stick to the official route.

288
00:18:00,723 --> 00:18:05,394
I may look like I'm just hanging around, but I'm actually helping residents.

289
00:18:05,961 --> 00:18:08,631
Hence the arcades and parlors while on patrol?

290
00:18:09,098 --> 00:18:13,269
You need to watch the world from different perspectives.

291
00:18:13,469 --> 00:18:15,805
Oh, a scale.

292
00:18:16,038 --> 00:18:17,973
Let's see how much we weigh.

293
00:18:18,941 --> 00:18:20,576
Building models, kids?

294
00:18:20,776 --> 00:18:24,914
But you shouldn't build them here. You're in people's way.

295
00:18:25,147 --> 00:18:27,116
-Sorry. -Sorry.

296
00:18:27,783 --> 00:18:30,619
Show me at the police station when you're done!

297
00:18:31,454 --> 00:18:32,955
All right, here we go.

298
00:18:34,156 --> 00:18:34,990
What the heck?

299
00:18:35,191 --> 00:18:35,991
What's wrong?

300
00:18:36,192 --> 00:18:38,994
It's glue. Those kids must have left it here.

301
00:18:40,162 --> 00:18:43,599
-I'm stuck. It's superglue! -What?!

302
00:18:44,133 --> 00:18:46,302
-Do something! -Okay!

303
00:18:47,269 --> 00:18:48,437
What are you doing?

304
00:18:48,637 --> 00:18:51,307
I'll lift you up. We have to get back to work.

305
00:18:53,509 --> 00:18:54,310
Huh?

306
00:18:56,011 --> 00:18:56,679
What's wrong?

307
00:18:56,912 --> 00:18:59,849
-Now my knees are stuck! -What?!

308
00:19:16,565 --> 00:19:18,167
A dump truck ploughed through!

309
00:19:28,177 --> 00:19:28,978
It's a hill!

310
00:19:30,946 --> 00:19:32,648
We're going faster!

311
00:19:33,983 --> 00:19:36,552
And he's totally a hunk so—

312
00:19:39,855 --> 00:19:40,890
What was that?

313
00:19:41,857 --> 00:19:44,193
I'm so embarrassed I could die!

314
00:19:46,562 --> 00:19:48,063
Cars! At the intersection!

315
00:19:48,564 --> 00:19:49,331
I wanna live!

316
00:19:49,999 --> 00:19:51,233
We gotta turn.

317
00:19:51,700 --> 00:19:52,835
How?

318
00:19:53,035 --> 00:19:56,972
We do a hang off! Shift your center of gravity. Like this!

319
00:19:58,240 --> 00:20:00,709
Hey, move that butt! Do you wanna die?

320
00:20:01,877 --> 00:20:03,145
I'm going again.

321
00:20:03,345 --> 00:20:05,214
One, two...

322
00:20:05,714 --> 00:20:06,615
Three!

323
00:20:06,849 --> 00:20:07,883
Good!

324
00:20:08,284 --> 00:20:11,153
We did it! It's just like skateboarding!

325
00:20:11,887 --> 00:20:14,623
You see, Miyaji? Playing around came in handy again.

326
00:20:14,857 --> 00:20:16,759
Ryotsu-san, behind you!

327
00:20:16,992 --> 00:20:18,894
Oh no, it's a church!

328
00:20:19,295 --> 00:20:21,764
I now pronounce you husband and wife—

329
00:20:24,567 --> 00:20:26,602
-Miyaji, hang off! To the right! -Okay!

330
00:20:28,170 --> 00:20:30,039
Congratulations!

331
00:20:31,273 --> 00:20:34,176
To disgrace the aisle like that...

332
00:20:35,845 --> 00:20:36,712
Amen.

333
00:20:39,949 --> 00:20:42,284
We did it. We made it to the main street.

334
00:20:42,484 --> 00:20:44,053
We've finally stopped.

335
00:20:44,253 --> 00:20:47,022
Aren't you ashamed to be seen like this in public?

336
00:20:47,223 --> 00:20:51,460
It's not our fault. Our legs are stuck.

337
00:20:51,861 --> 00:20:52,661
Huh?

338
00:20:53,629 --> 00:20:55,231
"KAMEARI SOGO BANK"

339
00:20:57,800 --> 00:20:58,968
It's a robbery!

340
00:21:02,304 --> 00:21:03,606
He's a bank robber!

341
00:21:03,806 --> 00:21:06,976
He thinks he can get away, huh? Miyaji, after him!

342
00:21:07,209 --> 00:21:08,978
Not while glued to this scale!

343
00:21:09,211 --> 00:21:10,746
No! We gotta catch him now.

344
00:21:10,946 --> 00:21:14,116
Think of how much money and manpower it'll cost otherwise!

345
00:21:15,050 --> 00:21:17,953
Patrol officers are crucial for the initial response!

346
00:21:19,655 --> 00:21:20,489
Got it!

347
00:21:20,689 --> 00:21:22,091
Right, let's go!

348
00:21:24,827 --> 00:21:26,829
Oh! Ryotsu-san, a car!

349
00:21:28,230 --> 00:21:30,065
Oh my gosh! Pervert!

350
00:21:30,266 --> 00:21:31,634
Follow that motorbike!

351
00:21:32,101 --> 00:21:32,902
Ew, no!

352
00:21:34,270 --> 00:21:36,472
-All right, we picked up some speed. -Yes!

353
00:21:37,306 --> 00:21:39,508
Oh, a small truck! Perfect.

354
00:21:43,846 --> 00:21:44,913
Where's the perp?

355
00:21:48,917 --> 00:21:49,852
He turned left!

356
00:21:50,085 --> 00:21:52,855
-All right, change lanes! Move that butt! -Got it!

357
00:21:53,088 --> 00:21:55,124
Ready, go!

358
00:21:56,692 --> 00:21:58,460
Uh oh! We went too much!

359
00:21:58,661 --> 00:21:59,795
Ryotsu-san, a car!

360
00:22:01,030 --> 00:22:04,166
Hello, good man. I may be naked, but I'm still a cop.

361
00:22:04,366 --> 00:22:06,101
Follow that motorcycle.

362
00:22:06,302 --> 00:22:09,038
Oh, you're Ryo-san from Kameari Park Police Station.

363
00:22:09,271 --> 00:22:11,540
-You know me? -Okay, leave it to me.

364
00:22:12,007 --> 00:22:13,709
Thanks for the help!

365
00:22:18,948 --> 00:22:22,151
All right, we've got him. The road's closed for roadworks.

366
00:22:22,351 --> 00:22:23,118
Ryotsu-san!

367
00:22:23,319 --> 00:22:24,353
Huh?

368
00:22:24,553 --> 00:22:26,355
My leg is coming unstuck!

369
00:22:26,555 --> 00:22:27,556
What?

370
00:22:30,960 --> 00:22:33,162
-He turned around. -He's coming this way!

371
00:22:37,533 --> 00:22:40,703
Stop resisting! Police!

372
00:22:43,138 --> 00:22:44,673
We did it!

373
00:22:45,541 --> 00:22:46,375
Where's Ryo-san?

374
00:22:51,313 --> 00:22:55,050
The man ran out of the bank in the third district.

375
00:22:55,551 --> 00:23:00,389
Wow, you really went all out to catch him.

376
00:23:00,589 --> 00:23:02,591
-Good job, Miyaji. -Thank you, sir.

377
00:23:03,058 --> 00:23:04,927
All right, all right.

378
00:23:05,694 --> 00:23:10,165
Hey, Ryotsu. What are you doing in that state?

379
00:23:11,867 --> 00:23:13,902
What happened to the bank robber?

380
00:23:14,470 --> 00:23:16,705
Miyaji made a flawless apprehend.

381
00:23:16,905 --> 00:23:19,074
He's getting the Superintendent's Award.

382
00:23:19,541 --> 00:23:21,343
What?! The Superintendent's Award?

383
00:23:21,543 --> 00:23:26,015
Miyaji! We'll split the money 40:60 between you and me!

384
00:23:26,415 --> 00:23:29,918
You moron! You're not getting any award!

385
00:23:30,119 --> 00:23:33,722
But I chased the robber with Miyaji...

386
00:23:34,223 --> 00:23:37,726
The Katsushika Police Department has been inundated with reports.

387
00:23:37,926 --> 00:23:39,762
Something about a perv on a scale.

388
00:23:40,262 --> 00:23:43,565
A written apology won't cut it this time! I'm docking your pay!

389
00:23:43,766 --> 00:23:47,269
What?! But Miyaji was butt-naked too!

390
00:23:47,770 --> 00:23:52,207
Ryo-chan, in situations like this, past actions speak louder than words.

391
00:23:52,408 --> 00:23:54,243
That's right, Ryotsu.

392
00:23:54,576 --> 00:23:57,746
Chief, that's not fair! You can't dock my pay!

393
00:23:58,080 --> 00:24:01,517
Chief! Chief! Chief!

394
00:24:03,085 --> 00:24:08,857
RYO-SAN'S DOLL, IN STORES NOW!
